Production| Duiven | Day shift | Aviation | Permanent position |

Do you enjoy hands-on work and are you comfortable performing precise, repetitive tasks? Would you like to work with equipment that is essential for aviation safety? Then this Production Employee position in Duiven might be a great opportunity for you.

What are you going to do?
As a Production Operator, you will assist with the inspection and testing of aircraft safety equipment. You will work in the Oxy department, where oxygen canisters used during emergency situations are inspected and checked. Your work ensures that all products meet strict aviation standards before they are returned to airlines.

You will follow clear step-by-step instructions in English. The work consists of repetitive tasks, so it is important that you are comfortable working in a structured environment and enjoy routine processes.

This is a full-time position (40 hours per week), Monday through Friday, from 7:00 AM to 4:00 PM. There is a strong possibility that the company will transition to a two-shift system in the future.

What do we offer?
- Salary between €2,900 and €3,600 gross per month;
- You will start directly with the company, meaning you will be employed directly by the client from day one.
- Opportunity for a permanent contract in the near future;
- A detailed training period of several months;
- Stable working hours and a structured environment;
- Travel allowance;
- A friendly team where colleagues know each other well;
- Opportunities to learn multiple departments over time.

Where will you work?
You will work for a specialized aviation safety company located in Duiven that inspects and maintains aircraft safety equipment for major international airlines. The company operates globally but maintains a close-knit team locally, with around 50 employees working together daily. Safety, teamwork and precision are essential. Because the company works with international customers, English is the main working langua

